Generate one complete Modelica model for this requirement:
Build a verifiable fluid-power robotic actuator system named PneuGripConserveE. The resulting scenario must make the following behavior testable: Complete a repeated actuation cycle while limiting hydraulic or pneumatic energy use. Represent the plant without omitting its structure. Two pneumatic cylinders with 0.035 m travel and 0.0012 m2 piston area drive opposing 0.8 kg gripper fingers. Two proportional air valves command the compressible chambers, with command magnitude bounded by 0.001 kg/s. Measure supply flow, pressure, actuator state, and accumulated energy or air mass. Include realistic return pressure, valve saturation, and thermal or compressibility effects. Apply energy-aware motion control with bounded performance degradation and a controlled 216 N load variation middle-third disturbance. Run at 250 Hz for 16 s and retain synchronized state, command, and sensor traces. Acceptance is fail-closed. Require all physical bounds, cycle completion, terminal error, and declared energy or air-use cap, primary tracking error below 0.018 m after 10.4 s, and no NaN or infinite physical, control, or estimator values. Treat facts not stated in this request as unknown rather than inventing them.

